            <ArticleTitle>Selective arterialization of the coronary venous system.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1458-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The idea of myocardial revascularization by means of grafting the coronary venous system is more than a century old; in cases of diffuse coronary artery disease, this may represent a valid therapeutic option. We present a challenging case in which a patient with an aberrant left coronary system and unstable angina underwent this type of procedure with good clinical results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
